```python
import re

EMAIL_RE = re.compile(
    r"^[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\.[A-Za-z]{2,}$"
)

def is_valid_email(email: str) -> bool:
    return bool(EMAIL_RE.match(email))
```

Checks for a name part, an `@`, a domain with a dot, and a letters-only ending like `.com`. Good enough for form checks, not a full spec check — real proof is sending a confirmation link.
